# Build output and run artifacts.
bin/
coverage.out

# bolt writes here; a run's artifacts belong to the run, not the repo. One
# directory per run, stamped with when it started, so `.bolt*` rather than a
# single name.
.bolt*/

# Working files for this project.
.ephemera/

# Session handoff. Ephemeral by design; state lives in the tracked documents.
START_HERE.md

# Parse trees of real commands, one directory each, rendered from the decisions
# log at ~/.local/state/qwark/decisions.jsonl. Generated rather than authored,
# and half a megabyte of SVG, so it is regenerated rather than stored:
#     ~/.projects/wrench/.ephemera/make-ast-gallery.sh example_graphs
example_graphs/

# This machine's hook registration. It names absolute paths that exist here and
# nowhere else (/etc/qwark/rules, and qwark on PATH), so it is a local
# arrangement rather than something to hand to whoever clones this.
# install/settings-fragment.json is the tracked account of what it should say.
.claude/settings.local.json

# The adopted jig links. `toolbox/jigs.yaml` declares the set; `link-jigs` makes
# them. They are ignored because in a built image the same files arrive from the
# anvil layer beneath, so a committed copy would be a third statement of one
# thing. A tracked symlink also stores its target path as content, which would
# encode where ../toolbox happens to sit.
#
# Named one at a time rather than as `bolt.*.yaml`, because that glob would also
# swallow `bolt.go-std-quality.definitions.yaml`, this project's own values for
# the shared jig's placeholders, which IS tracked and is the one part a shared
# definition must never carry.
bolt.common-quality.yaml
bolt.go-std-quality.yaml
bolt.secrets.yaml
adapters/
config/
